.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "train" "train"
.SH NAME
train \- Train the neuro-fuzzy model: one Takagi-Sugeno network per target gene.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fItrain(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Train the neuro-fuzzy model: one Takagi-Sugeno network per target gene.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- the untrained model created by \fBfuzzygene::build_fuzzygene\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the trained model object, or an R# error object when training fails
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Training is per gene and therefore parallelizable; a gene that cannot be fitted (constant
 expression, no candidate regulator, ill conditioned least squares) is recorded as skipped
 or failed instead of aborting the whole run. Use \fBfuzzygene::fuzzygene_report\fR to inspect
 the per gene diagnostics.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
